{"id": "EUVD-2026-93294", "enisaUuid": "29e49559-cda7-3169-b6e7-c4637f278411", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\ndrm/vc4: Use managed KMS polling to fix UAF on unbind\n\nvc4_kms_load() calls drm_kms_helper_poll_init() but the driver provides\nno matching drm_kms_helper_poll_fini(). The output poll work stays\nscheduled after unbind and runs on the freed drm_device:\n\n  # modprobe vc4; rmmod vc4; sleep 10\n  BUG: KASAN: slab-use-after-free in delayed_work_timer_fn\n  BUG: KASAN: slab-use-after-free in drm_client_dev_hotplug [drm]\n  Workqueue: events output_poll_execute [drm_kms_helper]\n  Allocated by task 171: __devm_drm_dev_alloc\n  Freed by task 262 (rmmod): drm_dev_put / component_del\n\nUse drmm_kms_helper_poll_init() so polling is finalized with the device,\nas other drivers do.", "datePublished": "2026-10-06T08:46:05", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T09:17:19", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/b6beee927e7f4e3142032ff91b2d0417cdddc0f6", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/cf0c4432bda37b02e7d430ff5017228ceb7caf0c", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/ee507691c18f9fee5d4751e295ab9a7ff31d59ae", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/7f9780df677370a19b4ec9764f13b1b82073e0d9", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/073a30d75f309812ed61af134f24ffef4107b13a"], "aliases": ["GHSA-fcmj-9h4r-58r4", "CVE-2026-98309"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.18, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "12d8b661-9685-3ea7-87d9-2391bc41b0c9", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.112"}, {"id": "199c2444-ffd3-3f58-841b-3c800987b2e2", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "c8b75bca92cbf064b9fa125fc74a85994452e935 <073a30d75f309812ed61af134f24ffef4107b13a"}, {"id": "5dcc9ac5-15ac-3ac7-887b-5da2aaee5e37", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "c8b75bca92cbf064b9fa125fc74a85994452e935 <b6beee927e7f4e3142032ff